    <div class="column">
      <h2 style="font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold;">8p Pick-up • Interest Rate • Mispricing</h2>
      <h3 style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">Interest Rate Pick-up: •222 bp</h3>
      <p>To find the interest rate pick-up, I found a bond with very similar characteristics in terms of rating, optionally and sector to that of Clear Channel, but changed the duration from 5.10 to that with a duration of 5.15.</p>
      <p><strong>Mispricing Pick-up: 3 bp</strong></p>
      <p>Sprint's bond is significantly undervalued, while the Clear Channel bond is trading at fair value. The mispricing basis point pick-up is found from substituting the other pick-up.</p>
      <p><strong>Callability Schedule</strong></p>
      <p>Sprint's first bond becomes callable as of <span data-field="date_callable_sprint">{{ date_callable_sprint }}</span>, 2024 at the price of <span data-field="price_callable_sprint">{{ price_callable_sprint }}</span>. It can be called with a 30 day minimum notice. They may be called in part or in full.</p>
      <p><strong>Credit Analysis</strong></p>
      <p>It is important to closely examine the financial stability of Sprint when considering purchasing it for our portfolio. Since 2006, profitability has not been a strength of Sprint's. However, it's part of their strategy to undercut their larger competitors to gain subscribers. Now that Sprint has managed to gain on their competition, they are beginning to change their original game plan and compete with the larger competitors at a profitable pricing strategy.</p>
      <p>One of the most concerning factors of Sprint is their high level of debt with <span data-field="debt_level_sprint">{{ debt_level_sprint }}</span> and a debt to equity ratio of <span data-field="debt_equity_sprint">{{ debt_equity_sprint }}</span>. This level, however, is not unusual. Sprint believes itself to be a smaller competitor, and it is a smaller competitor.</p>
      <p>I made which a high debt of <span data-field="debt_amount_sprint">{{ debt_amount_sprint }}</span> billion and a debt to equity of <span data-field="debt_equity_amount_sprint">{{ debt_equity_amount_sprint }}</span>. For this reason, Sprint could be considered risky if we were not for their recent move toward a profitable strategy. Sprint is getting its business plan of undercutting competitors and will now catch up in profitability. Since June 2016, Sprint's profitability has increased by 19 percent, proving that it has a positive trend. Going forward, the price received will be risk-well if without actually the concern of Sprint defaulting. A pro forma income statement and statement of cash flows has been generated to show estimated growth.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="column">
      <p>debt levels and higher duration, it is extremely unlikely that Sprint would default on their debt or be unable to pay it back.</p>
      <h3 style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">Credit Watch</h3>
      <p>Sprint is not under any credit watch under any rating agency at this time.</p>
