  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p style="font-weight: bold;">Valuation: Sales Franchise Value Model.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Sales Franchise valuation is often used when dealing with companies that are able to repeat its business model at a higher profit margin. This model distinguishes between a company's current profit margin and the margin that can be derived from future opportunities. The underlying assumption for Match Group Inc. is that it will be able to improve its profit margin by lowering its operating costs while increasing its total revenue via Tinder's explosive growth. Using its current profit margin of <span data-field="current_profit_margin">{{ current_profit_margin }}</span>, we determined the median fair value for Match.com to be <span data-field="median_fair_value">{{ median_fair_value }}</span>, undervalued by <span data-field="undervaluation_percentage">{{ undervaluation_percentage }}</span> percent.</p>
