<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: left; font-size: 10pt;">STETSON UNIVERSITY</div>
  <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 20px;">
    <div style="font-size: 24pt; font-weight: bold;">VR Index (VR4)</div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 30px;">
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <div class="sub-heading">by: <span data-field="author_name">{{ author_name }}</span></div>
      <div class="section-title">Introduction</div>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">The idea of virtual reality (VR) dates back to the early 1800's. Arthur Whitney, in 1838, is often credited with creating the first stereoscope, which created three-dimensional images by placing two slightly different two-dimensional photographs in front of each eye.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Early VR as revolutionary as this may sound, VR is still in its infant stage. However, the sky is the limit for this technology. The VR industry is expected to grow at a compound annual growth rate of <span data-field="growth_rate_vr">{{ growth_rate_vr }}</span> percent over the next decade.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">The market for VR is expected to reach a value of <span data-field="market_value_vr">{{ market_value_vr }}</span> by <span data-field="year_vr">{{ year_vr }}</span>.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <div class="section-title">Industry</div>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">VR has started to penetrate a wide variety of industries. As a result, several industry research and consulting firms have started tracking the economic impact of this technology. Some are less conservative than others, but the consensus is that the market is poised for massive growth.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">The market is expected to grow at a compound annual growth rate of <span data-field="growth_rate_industry">{{ growth_rate_industry }}</span> percent over the next five years. This will be driven by the increasing adoption of VR in various sectors.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">The market is expected to reach a value of <span data-field="market_value_industry">{{ market_value_industry }}</span> by <span data-field="year_industry">{{ year_industry }}</span>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 30px;">
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <div class="section-title">Investment Rationale</div>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">VR is an interesting case because it uses existing technology, such as mobile devices, but has vastly different applications on a very broad user base.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">The market is currently in a phase of early adoption, and the consumer level. The problem is that consumers won't purchase VR hardware until there is a compelling reason to do so, and the content ecosystem is not yet mature enough to ramp up production until an ample hardware base exists in the market. What we have is the classic chicken and egg scenario.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <div class="section-title">Display Technology</div>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Display technology is another integral part of VR adoption. Because VR headsets place screens less than an inch from the user's eyes, crisp and powerful displays are necessary for viewing VR content. This means that the newly introduced OLED technology will gradually phase out the traditional LCD.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">The limitations of LCD technology in VR application will be overcome by the introduction of OLED. OLED allows for a much higher contrast ratio and deeper blacks, which are crucial for an immersive VR experience.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">The market for OLED displays is expected to reach a value of <span data-field="oled_market_value">{{ oled_market_value }}</span> by <span data-field="oled_year">{{ oled_year }}</span>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Proprietary VR headsets, like the <span data-field="headset_name">{{ headset_name }}</span>, can be used to create immersive experiences. These devices are becoming more sophisticated, offering higher resolution and wider fields of view. This is driving the demand for VR content and applications.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 40px;">
